<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<fortificationDefine>
  <fortificationEum name="Abatis" food="100" wood="1200" stone="0" iron="150" repairRateRequest="6" time="120" space="2" range="5000" desc="Abatises are wooden barricades which are used to stop horsemen." wikiDesc="An obstacle formed from the branches of trees laid in a row, with the points directed toward the enemy. The trees are usually interlaced or tied with wire. An Abatis can be used alone or in combination with wire entanglements and other obstacles. Abatisses are used in war to keep the approaching enemy under fire for as long as possible. Most useful against highly mobilised troops such as horsemen." typeId="15" life="0" defence="0" attack="0" exp="1675"/>
  <fortificationEum name="Archer's Tower" food="200" wood="2000" stone="1000" iron="500" repairRateRequest="3" time="180" space="3" range="1300" desc="Towers built on the city walls to provide a vantage point to shoot enemies." wikiDesc="Archers formed a significant element of many medieval armies, though their numbers, tactical deployment and effectiveness varied widely. An Archer’s tower is built on walls, which allow a high standing point. Squarely built up into the sky, and with open sight in all directions, it allows archers to defend their city more flexibly." typeId="16" life="2000" defence="360" attack="300" exp="15450"/>
  <fortificationEum name="Defensive Trebuchet" food="600" wood="0" stone="8000" iron="0" repairRateRequest="8" time="600" space="5" range="5000" desc="Excellent at destroying enemy siege weapons, a trebuchet will only get one shot per battle and must then be rebuilt and reloaded." wikiDesc="Excellent at destroying enemy siege weapons, a trebuchet will only get one shot per battle and must then be rebuilt and reloaded." typeId="18" life="0" defence="0" attack="800" exp="2200"/>
  <fortificationEum name="Rolling log" food="300" wood="6000" stone="0" iron="0" repairRateRequest="7" time="360" space="4" range="1300" desc="Huge lengthy logs roll down to crush your enemies to death." wikiDesc="The Rollinglog is believed to be an assistant tool for the construction of Pyramids. It wasn’t until long after medieval times that these logs were applied to warfare. As usual, most castles or forts were built on a mountain or hill, a naturally formed slope that made it hard to attack. Offenders would be at the mercy of rolling logs, as they increased in speed the further they tumbled down a hill." typeId="17" life="0" defence="0" attack="500" exp="6300"/>
  <fortificationEum name="Trap" food="50" wood="500" stone="100" iron="50" repairRateRequest="5" time="60" space="1" range="5000" desc="A trap is a defensive tool used to attack an enemy by surprise.  It is effective against rival infantry." wikiDesc="A trap is a device set up to be triggered by an unsuspecting victim. As the word 'trap' implies, they usually have some form of bait designed to lure the victim towards it. In other cases, however, the trap is set to be triggered when the victim performs an everyday action such as opening a door. Traps were usually made of wood which was cheap in price and easily accessed." typeId="14" life="0" defence="0" attack="0" exp="875"/>
</fortificationDefine>